      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1327614788,
      "text": "Girardinia diversifolia, commonly known as the Himalayan nettle or Nilghiri nettle, is a plant species with a wide native range across southern and eastern Asia and across most of tropical Africa and Madagascar. It grows naturally at elevations between 100 and 2,800 metres."
    },
